{
  "manufacturer": "WOLF",
  "manufacturer_slug": "wolf",
  "model": "WRS-K air handling unit controller - BACnet interface",
  "model_slug": "wrs-k-bacnet-interface",
  "aliases": [
    "WOLF WRS-K BACnet",
    "Rozhraní BACnet pro WRS-K",
    "Rozhranie BACnet pre WRS-K",
    "KLM-S",
    "KLM-L",
    "KLM-XL"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Air handling unit controller",
  "applies_to": "WOLF air handling and ventilation units with the WRS-K regulator (KLM-S, KLM-L, KLM-XL air-handling modules) fitted with the BACnet interface card.",
  "summary": "The BACnet interface card for WOLF's WRS-K air-handling controller gives BACnet IP (or BACnet Ethernet) access to the unit. It publishes fixed binary and analog values: operating states and outputs, temperatures, humidity, pressures and airflows, active special modes, one binary value per alarm, and a write section with BMS setpoints, setpoint offsets, the operating mode, BMS outdoor/room temperature, an electric heater power limit and remote alarm reset.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": "WRS-K 5.4-5.8 (some objects need the later versions)",
  "default_device_instance": 77000,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Taken from section 7 (Interface description) of WOLF's Czech-language BACnet interface manual for the WRS-K (3065168, 2024-05); object types, instances, object names and units are printed in the tables, the descriptions there are Czech.",
    "Access follows the manual's sections: 7.1 read-only access, 7.2 write access. AV 1006 Operation_Mode is listed in both and is writable.",
    "The manual prints BV 90 twice: as Adiabatic_Cooling_Enable (air-heater thermostat) in the read table and as Alarm_Reset_BMS (WRS-K 5.7.000+) in the write section. Only the Alarm_Reset_BMS entry is kept; check on site.",
    "BV 87 and BV 90 both carry the name Adiabatic_Cooling_Enable in the read table; AV 1092 and AV 1093 are both printed as Pressure_Filter_SUP3. Names are kept as printed.",
    "Airflow objects marked in the manual (AV 1004/1005, 1010/1011, 1017/1018, 1022/1023) carry the real value divided by 10.",
    "Several objects need a minimum WRS-K software version (5.4.000 to 5.8.000), as footnoted in the manual."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set AV 1006 Operation_Mode to 2 (BMS operation) and write the BMS setpoints (AV 15 temperature, AV 16/17 fan speeds or AV 1015/1016 pressure, AV 1014 fan step). In manual or weekly-program mode, adjust with the Offset objects instead. Read BV 5 Status_AHU, the supply and room temperatures, and BV 1 Alarm_General plus the individual alarm BVs.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AV 1006",
        "name": "Operation_Mode",
        "why": "Operating mode: 0 manual, 1 weekly program, 2 BMS"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1014",
        "name": "Setpoint_Fan_Step_BMS",
        "why": "Unit on/off in BMS mode: 1 = off, 2 = on"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 15",
        "name": "Setpoint_Temperature_BMS",
        "why": "Temperature setpoint from the BMS, °C"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 16",
        "name": "Setpoint_Speed_SUP_BMS",
        "why": "Supply fan speed setpoint from the BMS, %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 17",
        "name": "Setpoint_Speed_ETA_BMS",
        "why": "Extract fan speed setpoint from the BMS, %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 90",
        "name": "Alarm_Reset_BMS",
        "why": "Remote alarm reset (enable in service menu)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 5",
        "name": "Status_AHU",
        "why": "Unit status (1 = running)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1",
        "name": "Temperature_SUP",
        "why": "Supply air temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 3",
        "name": "Temperature_Room",
        "why": "Room temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 1",
        "name": "Alarm_General",
        "why": "Common fault"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "AV 1006 Operation_Mode selects 0 = manual operation, 1 = weekly program, 2 = BMS operation. In BMS operation the _BMS setpoint objects apply and AV 1014 Setpoint_Fan_Step_BMS switches the unit (1 = off, 2 = on); in manual or weekly-program mode the Offset_..._BMS objects shift the local setpoints. Values outside the allowed range are rejected and the old value is kept.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": "AV 37 Temperature_Outdoor_BMS and AV 71 Temperature_Room_BMS take outdoor and room temperature from the BMS once enabled in the service menu. Each value is plausibility-checked: outside -50 to 60 °C, or unchanged by at least 0.1 K for 24 hours, raises an alarm.",
    "setup": [
      "Factory device instance 77000; choose BACnet IP or BACnet Ethernet on the card's BACnet web page.",
      "Out of the box the card's web pages answer at 172.16.0.1 (factory login in the manual); IP settings are on Configuration > Network.",
      "An EDE file for the interface is offered on wolf.eu."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "AV 1055 Max_Power_Eheater is held in controller memory and saved to permanent memory only hourly, to spare the memory cells; after a power cut the last saved value applies until a new one is sent.",
      "With an active setpoint device on the unit, the temperature setpoint cannot be changed over the interface.",
      "In BMS operation a supply fan speed or pressure setpoint of 0 also sets the extract setpoint to 0.",
      "Remote alarm reset (BV 90) must be enabled by a service technician and is only offered on some series (CGL2 edu, CFL edu)."
    ]
  },
